; Interprets: 3GPP TS 29.272
;; What TS 29.272's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order: the information-element tables' rows and the procedure
;; clauses of 5, 5A and 6, the base protocol's use in 7.1 and 7.2, the AVP
;; clauses of 7.3, then the result codes of 7.4. A clause pointing at
;; another document for a layout is an `element`; a rule depending on an
;; earlier message, a feature, the node or the subscriber is `text-only`.


;; The conditions of the C rows of the information-element tables, scoped to
;; the command each table describes. A row only available on its node's say
;; ("if available") states no rule.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-ula-flags
; AVP: ULA-Flags
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present only when the Result-Code AVP is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-subscription-data
; AVP: Subscription-Data
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if success is reported, unless an explicit \"skip subscriber data\" indication was present in the request."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/ULR-Flags bit "Skip Subscriber Data"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-sgsn-number
; AVP: SGSN-Number
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present when the message is sent on the S6d interface and the SGSN supports LCS (using MAP based Lg interface) or SMS functionalities or the Gs interface."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-ue-srvcc-capability
; AVP: UE-SRVCC-Capability
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"shall be present if the MME or the SGSN supports SRVCC and this information is available to the MME or the SGSN."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-mme-number-for-mt-sms
; AVP: MME-Number-for-MT-SMS
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present when the MME supports SMS in MME and wishes to provide SMS in MME."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-sms-register-request
; AVP: SMS-Register-Request
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present when the MME supports SMS in MME and requests to be registered for SMS."
"It shall be present when the SGSN supports \"SMS in SGSN\" as defined in clause 5.3.18 in 23.060 [12], and requests to be registered for SMS."
    text-only


;; An IMSI is at most 15 digits, MCC's 3, MNC's 2 or 3 and the MSIN's
;; (TS 23.003 clause 2.2), carried as text.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain the user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


;; Each answer's Result row: "This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the
;; 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP".
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-terminal-information
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Within this Information Element, only the IMEI and the Software-Version AVPs shall be used on the S6a/S6d interface."
    members only IMEI Software-Version


;; An Active-APN without Specific-APN-Info is an explicitly subscribed
;; APN's: the Wildcard APN's carries the Specific-APN-Info listing the APNs
;; in use (clause 7.3.82), and an explicit APN carries none.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: active-apn-explicit-service-selection
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Within: Active-APN
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"For the case of explicitly subscribed APNs, the following information shall be present: - Context-Identifier: context id of subscribed APN in use - Service-Selection: name of subscribed APN in use - MIP6-Agent-Info: including PDN GW identity in use for subscribed APN - Visited-Network-Identifier: identifies the PLMN where the PDN GW was allocated"
"For the case of the Wildcard APN, the following information shall be present: - Context-Identifier: context id of the Wildcard APN - Specific-APN-Info: list of APN-in use and related PDN GW identity when the subscribed APN is the wildcard APN"
    present-if not Specific-APN-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: active-apn-explicit-mip6-agent-info
; AVP: MIP6-Agent-Info
; Within: Active-APN
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"For the case of explicitly subscribed APNs, the following information shall be present: - Context-Identifier: context id of subscribed APN in use - Service-Selection: name of subscribed APN in use - MIP6-Agent-Info: including PDN GW identity in use for subscribed APN - Visited-Network-Identifier: identifies the PLMN where the PDN GW was allocated"
"For the case of the Wildcard APN, the following information shall be present: - Context-Identifier: context id of the Wildcard APN - Specific-APN-Info: list of APN-in use and related PDN GW identity when the subscribed APN is the wildcard APN"
    present-if not Specific-APN-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: active-apn-explicit-visited-network-identifier
; AVP: Visited-Network-Identifier
; Within: Active-APN
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"For the case of explicitly subscribed APNs, the following information shall be present: - Context-Identifier: context id of subscribed APN in use - Service-Selection: name of subscribed APN in use - MIP6-Agent-Info: including PDN GW identity in use for subscribed APN - Visited-Network-Identifier: identifies the PLMN where the PDN GW was allocated"
"For the case of the Wildcard APN, the following information shall be present: - Context-Identifier: context id of the Wildcard APN - Specific-APN-Info: list of APN-in use and related PDN GW identity when the subscribed APN is the wildcard APN"
    present-if not Specific-APN-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-sf-provisional-indication
; AVP: SF-Provisional-Indication
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 19.6.0
"This information element may only be included if the SF-ULR-Timestamp is present."
    requires SF-ULR-Timestamp


;; Each Error-Diagnostic value goes with one Experimental-Result-Code under
;; the 3GPP vendor (clause 7.3.128): GPRS_DATA_SUBSCRIBED and
;; NO_GPRS_DATA_SUBSCRIBED with DIAMETER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_EPS_SUBSCRIPTION, the
;; three ODB values with DIAMETER_ERROR_ROAMING_NOT_ALLOWED.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-error-diagnostic
; AVP: Error-Diagnostic
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If the Experimental Result indicates \"Unknown EPS Subscription\", Error Diagnostic may be present to indicate whether or not GPRS subscription data are subscribed (i.e. whether or not Network Access Mode stored in the HSS indicates that only circuit service is allowed)."
"If the Experimental Result indicates \"Roaming Not Allowed\", and the Update Location is rejected due to ODB, Error Diagnostic may be present to indicate the specific type of ODB."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415 and Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code in DIAMETER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_EPS_SUBSCRIPTION,
        DIAMETER_ERROR_ROAMING_NOT_ALLOWED
    values 0, 1 if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_EPS_SUBSCRIPTION
    values 2, 3, 4 if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_ROAMING_NOT_ALLOWED


;; What the HSS puts in the subscription data of a ULA, a complete profile
;; (table 5.2.1.1.1/2); an IDR's is the part changed, and is read in clause
;; 5.2.2.1.3.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-subscription-data-contents
; AVP: Subscription-Data
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1.3
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Subscriber-Status AVP shall be present in the Subscription-Data AVP when sent within a ULA."
    requires Subscription-Data/Subscriber-Status
"If the value \"OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING\" is sent, the Operator-Determined-Barring AVP or HPLMN-ODB AVP shall also be present in the Subscription-Data AVP, or vice versa."
    requires not Subscription-Data/Subscriber-Status = OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING or Subscription-Data/Operator-Determined-Barring or Subscription-Data/HPLMN-ODB
    requires not Subscription-Data/Operator-Determined-Barring or Subscription-Data/Subscriber-Status = OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING
    requires not Subscription-Data/HPLMN-ODB or Subscription-Data/Subscriber-Status = OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING
"The AMBR AVP shall be present in the Subscription-Data AVP when the APN-Configuration-Profile AVP is sent within a ULA (as part of the Subscription-Data AVP)"
    requires not Subscription-Data/APN-Configuration-Profile or Subscription-Data/AMBR
"When the APN-Configuration-Profile AVP is present in the Subscription-Data AVP sent within a ULA, the AVP shall contain at least the default APN Configuration and a Context-Identifier AVP that identifies the per subscriber's default APN configuration."
"The default APN Configuration shall not contain the Wildcard APN (see TS 23.003 [3], clause 9.2); the default APN shall always contain an explicit APN."
    text-only
"If the Update Location Request includes an equivalent PLMN list, the HSS shall return the CSG list (if any) for each equivalent PLMN to the MME with the subscription data, and Visited-PLMN-Id AVP shall be present in the CSG-Subscription-Data AVP to indicate the corresponding PLMN."
    text-only


;; Every APN-Configuration of a profile, in a ULA as in an IDR: the profile
;; is carried in Subscription-Data alone, and Subscription-Data in these two
;; commands alone. Clause 5.2.2.1.3 says the same of the IDR, a block below
;; pinning its sentence to this rule.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-apn-configuration-qos-and-ambr
; AVP: APN-Configuration
; Within: APN-Configuration-Profile
; Section: 5.2.1.1.3
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"The EPS-Subscribed-QoS-Profile AVP and the AMBR AVP shall be present in the APN-Configuration AVP when the APN-Configuration AVP is sent in the APN-Configuration-Profile AVP and when the APN-Configuration-Profile AVP is sent within a ULA (as part of the Subscription-Data AVP)."
    members at-least-one EPS-Subscribed-QoS-Profile
    members at-least-one AMBR


;; A pre-Release-8 HSS's IWF clears the bit (clause 7.3.8), and no message
;; says the HSS is one.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-separation-indication
; AVP: ULA-Flags
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1.3
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If a Result Code of DIAMETER_SUCCESS is returned, the HSS shall set the Separation Indication in the response."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: clr-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Cancel-Location-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.2.1
; Table: 5.2.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain the user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pua-pua-flags
; AVP: PUA-Flags
; Command: Purge-UE-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.3.1
; Table: 5.2.1.3.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present only when the Result-Code AVP is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pur-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Purge-UE-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.3.1
; Table: 5.2.1.3.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pua-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Purge-UE-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.3.1
; Table: 5.2.1.3.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pur-eps-location-information
; AVP: EPS-Location-Information
; Command: Purge-UE-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.3.1
; Table: 5.2.1.3.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This Information Element shall contain the last known EPS-Location Information of the purged UE. Shall be present if available."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-ims-voice-over-ps-sessions-supported
; AVP: IMS-Voice-Over-PS-Sessions-Supported
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If the UE is in detached state, this information element shall not be included in the response."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-last-ue-activity-time
; AVP: Last-UE-Activity-Time
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If the UE is in detached state, this information element shall not be included in the response."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-rat-type
; AVP: RAT-Type
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If the UE is in detached state, this information element shall not be included in the response."
    text-only


;; What the IDR asked for, read from its IDR-Flags and Subscription-Data,
;; holds of a success's answer: one reporting an error carries none of it.
;; The Local Time Zone is the exception: clause 5.2.2.1.2 has the MME or
;; SGSN provide it "if supported", which no message shows.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-eps-user-state
; AVP: EPS-User-State
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if EPS user state was requested within IDR."
    present-if request/IDR-Flags bit "EPS User State Request" and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-eps-location-information
; AVP: EPS-Location-Information
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if EPS location information was requested within IDR."
    present-if request/IDR-Flags bit "EPS Location Information Request" and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-local-time-zone
; AVP: Local-Time-Zone
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if the Local Time Zone was requested within IDR."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-monitoring-event-report
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if Monitoring event configuration is included within IDR and any of the requested Monitoring events are available to be reported."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-monitoring-event-config-status
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Config-Status
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This Information Element shall be present if Monitoring event configuration is included in IDR."
    present-if request/Subscription-Data/Monitoring-Event-Configuration and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: idr-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain the user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; "only the \"Current Location Request\" bit set", as the parenthesis reads
;; it: without the EPS Location Information Request bit. An unknown IMSI's
;; answer carries DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN in Experimental-Result
;; instead, so the rule says no success, not which Result-Code.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ida-current-location-alone
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"When receiving the IDR-Flags with only the \"Current Location Request\" bit set (i.e. the \"EPS Location Information Request\" bit is not set), the MME or SGSN or combined MME/SGSN shall set the Result-Code to DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY."
    excludes Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and request/IDR-Flags bit "Current Location Request" and not request/IDR-Flags bit "EPS Location Information Request"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: idr-subscription-data-odb
; AVP: Subscription-Data
; Command: Insert-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.1.3
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If Subscriber-Status AVP is present and set to OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING, the Operator-Determined-Barring AVP or HPLMN-ODB AVP shall also be present in the Subscription-Data AVP."
    requires not Subscription-Data/Subscriber-Status = OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING or Subscription-Data/Operator-Determined-Barring or Subscription-Data/HPLMN-ODB
"The default APN Configuration shall not contain the Wildcard APN (see TS 23.003 [3], clause 9.2); the default APN shall always contain an explicit APN."
    text-only


;; The IDR's sentence, held by the rule of clause 5.2.1.1.3's block on the
;; same scope, which reads every APN-Configuration-Profile.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: idr-apn-configuration-qos-and-ambr
; AVP: APN-Configuration
; Within: APN-Configuration-Profile
; Section: 5.2.2.1.3
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"The EPS-Subscribed-QoS-Profile AVP and the AMBR AVP shall be present in the APN-Configuration AVP when the APN-Configuration AVP is sent in the APN-Configuration-Profile AVP and when the APN-Configuration-Profile AVP is sent within a IDR (as part of the Subscription-Data AVP)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-trace-reference
; AVP: Trace-Reference
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This element shall be present only if the \"Trace Data Withdrawal\" bit is set in the DSR-Flags."
    requires DSR-Flags bit "Trace Data Withdrawal"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-context-identifier
; AVP: Context-Identifier
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This element shall be present only if the \"PDN subscription contexts Withdrawal\" bit or the \"PDP context withdrawal\" bit is set in the DSR-Flags."
    requires DSR-Flags bit "PDN subscription contexts Withdrawal" or DSR-Flags bit "PDP contexts Withdrawal"
"In the \"PDN subscription contexts Withdrawal\" case, the Context-Identifier shall not be associated with the default APN configuration."
    text-only
"For the compatibility with the MAP protocol as defined in the TS 29.002 [24], this parameter shall not have a value of zero."
    exclude 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-ts-code
; AVP: TS-Code
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This element shall be present only if the \"SMS Withdrawal\" bit is set in the DSR-Flags and the SMS related teleservice codes are to be deleted."
    requires DSR-Flags bit "SMS Withdrawal"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-ss-code
; AVP: SS-Code
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This element shall be present only if the \"SMS Withdrawal\" bit is set or the \"LCS Withdrawal\" bit is set in the DSR-Flags."
    requires DSR-Flags bit "SMS Withdrawal" or DSR-Flags bit "LCS Withdrawal"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-scef-id
; AVP: SCEF-ID
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This element shall be present if the \"Delete monitoring events\" bit is set in the DSR-Flags."
    present-if DSR-Flags bit "Delete monitoring events"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-edrx-related-rat
; AVP: eDRX-Related-RAT
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This element shall be present only if the \"eDRX-Cycle-Length-Withdrawal\" bit is set in the DSR-Flags and the corresponding eDRX Cycle Lengths are to be deleted."
    requires DSR-Flags bit eDRX-Cycle-Length-Withdrawal


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain the user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsa-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; The row names the IE External-Identifiers; the command carries them as
;; External-Identifier AVPs. The row is O, not C.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dsr-external-identifier
; AVP: External-Identifier
; Command: Delete-Subscriber-Data-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.2.2.1
; Table: 5.2.2.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This IE shall be absent if the \"External-Identifier-Withdrawal\" bit is not set in the DSR-Flags."
    requires DSR-Flags bit External-Identifier-Withdrawal


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aia-ue-usage-type
; AVP: UE-Usage-Type
; Command: Authentication-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.3.1.1
; Table: 5.2.3.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This IE shall be present if the HSS supports the Dedicated Core Networks feature, and the \"Send UE Usage Type\" flag was set in the AIR-Flags AVP in the AIR command, and this information is available in the user subscription."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: air-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Authentication-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.3.1.1
; Table: 5.2.3.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain the user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aia-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Authentication-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.3.1.1
; Table: 5.2.3.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aia-error-diagnostic
; AVP: Error-Diagnostic
; Command: Authentication-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.3.1.1
; Table: 5.2.3.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If the Experimental Result indicated \"Unknown EPS Subscription\", Error Diagnostic may be present to indicate whether or not GPRS subscription data are subscribed (i.e. whether or not Network Access Mode stored in the HSS indicates that only CS service is allowed)."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415 and Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_EPS_SUBSCRIPTION
    values 0, 1 if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_EPS_SUBSCRIPTION


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: air-requested-authentication-info-exclusive
; AVP: Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info
; Command: Authentication-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.3.1.2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Re-Synchronization Information shall not be present in both the Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info AVP and the Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info AVP."
    excludes Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info/Re-Synchronization-Info and Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info/Re-Synchronization-Info
"The Immediate-Response-Preferred AVP shall not be present in both the Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info AVP and the Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info AVP."
    excludes Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info/Immediate-Response-Preferred and Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info/Immediate-Response-Preferred


;; Whether more than one vector of a kind, or of all kinds, is carried has
;; no form: no rule counts AVPs.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aia-authentication-info-resynchronization
; AVP: Authentication-Info
; Command: Authentication-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.3.1.3
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If both the Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info AVP and the Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info AVP are in the request, and both of them include the Re-Synchronization-Info AVP, the HSS shall not check the AUTS parameter and return the result code of DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY."
"Any authentication vectors shall not be sent by the HSS to the requesting node in the response."
    absent-if request/Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info/Re-Synchronization-Info and request/Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info/Re-Synchronization-Info
"If more than one EPS or UTRAN or GERAN Vector is to be included within one Authentication-Info AVP, the Item-Number AVP shall be present within each Vector."
    text-only


;; An error found before, such as DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN in
;; Experimental-Result, answers otherwise: the rule says no success.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aia-resynchronization-twice
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Authentication-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.3.1.3
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If both the Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info AVP and the Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info AVP are in the request, and both of them include the Re-Synchronization-Info AVP, the HSS shall not check the AUTS parameter and return the result code of DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY."
    excludes Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and request/Requested-EUTRAN-Authentication-Info/Re-Synchronization-Info and request/Requested-UTRAN-GERAN-Authentication-Info/Re-Synchronization-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rsa-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Reset-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.4.1.1
; Table: 5.2.4.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rsr-subscription-data
; AVP: Subscription-Data
; Command: Reset-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.4.1.1
; Table: 5.2.4.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Shall be absent if Subscription-Data-Deletion AVP is present. Shall be absent if Reset-ID AVP is absent"
    excludes Subscription-Data-Deletion
    requires Reset-ID


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rsr-subscription-data-deletion
; AVP: Subscription-Data-Deletion
; Command: Reset-Request
; Application-ID: 16777251
; Section: 5.2.4.1.1
; Table: 5.2.4.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Shall be absent if Subscription-Data AVP is present. Shall be absent if Reset-ID AVP is absent"
    excludes Subscription-Data
    requires Reset-ID


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-terminal-information
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Within this Information Element, only the IMEI and the Software-Version AVPs shall be used on the S6a/S6d interface."
    members only IMEI Software-Version


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-mip6-agent-info
; AVP: MIP6-Agent-Info
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if a new PDN-GW has been selected and the subscriber is allowed handover to non 3GPP access or 5GS interworking without N26 interface enabled."
    text-only
"For establishment of emergency PDN connections, this IE shall contain the identity of the PDN-GW used to establish those PDN connections."
    present-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


;; The Emergency-Services row has the MME include the AVP, its
;; Emergency-Indication set, to notify a new PDN-GW for an emergency PDN
;; connection, "whose identify is conveyed in the \"PDN GW Identity\" IE".
;;
;; The PDN GW Identity is MIP6-Agent-Info, its FQDN MIP-Home-Agent-Host's
;; Destination-Host.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-visited-network-identifier
; AVP: Visited-Network-Identifier
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present when the PDN GW Identity is present and does not contain an FQDN."
    present-if MIP6-Agent-Info and not MIP6-Agent-Info/MIP-Home-Agent-Host


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-service-selection
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"For establishment of non-emergency PDN connections, it shall be present if the selected PDN-GW is present and is particular for one specific APN and not common to all the APNs."
    text-only
"For establishment of emergency PDN connections (i.e., the Emergency-Services AVP is present, with the Emergency-Indication flag set), this AVP shall be left absent."
    absent-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-alert-reason
; AVP: Alert-Reason
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present when notifying the HSS about the presence of the UE or the UE has memory capacity available to receive one or more short messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-ue-srvcc-capability
; AVP: UE-SRVCC-Capability
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"If the MME/SGSN supports SRVCC and the UE SRVCC Capability has changed, the MME or SGSN shall include the new UE SRVCC Capability in the request."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-nor-flags
; AVP: NOR-Flags
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Absence of this information element shall be interpreted as all bits set to 0."
    default 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-homogeneous-support
; AVP: Homogeneous-Support-of-IMS-Voice-Over-PS-Sessions
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This Information Element shall be present if Homogeneous Support of IMS Voice Over PS Sessions is modified to one of the values \"SUPPORTED\" or \"NOT_SUPPORTED\"."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-monitoring-event-config-status
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Config-Status
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall be present if the MME/SGSN sends the Notify Request after receiving the Configuration-Information-Answer from the IWK-SCEF."
"This information element shall also be present if any of the monitoring events configurations received in ULA failed and shall only contain the monitoring event configuration status of those events whose detection could not be started at the MME/SGSN."
"This information element shall also be present if the MME or SGSN determines that a Monitoring Event Configuration for a UE is to be deleted in the HSS (i.e. SCEF responds to a Monitoring Event Report with DIAMETER_ERROR_SCEF_REFERENCE_ID_UNKNOWN)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-emergency-services
; AVP: Emergency-Services
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"The MME shall include this information element, and set the Emergency-Indication flag, to notify the HSS that a new PDN-GW has been selected for the establishment of an emergency PDN connection"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain the user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: noa-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Notify-Answer
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nor-context-identifier
; AVP: Context-Identifier
; Command: Notify-Request
; Section: 5.2.5.1.1
; Table: 5.2.5.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"For the compatibility with the MAP protocol as defined in the TS 29.002 [24], this parameter shall not have a value of zero."
    exclude 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: uvr-sgsn-number
; AVP: SGSN-Number
; Command: Update-VCSG-Location-Request
; Section: 5A.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5A.2.1.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present when the message is sent on the S7d interface."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: uva-vplmn-csg-subscription-data
; AVP: VPLMN-CSG-Subscription-Data
; Command: Update-VCSG-Location-Answer
; Section: 5A.2.1.1.1
; Table: 5A.2.1.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if success is reported, unless an explicit \"skip subscriber data\" indication was present in the request or the Temporary Empty VPLMN CSG Subscription Data flag is set."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/UVR-Flags bit "Skip Subscriber Data" and not UVA-Flags bit "Temporary Empty VPLMN CSG Subscription Data"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
