; AVP: Equipment-Status
; Command: ME-Identity-Check-Answer
; Section: 6.2.1.1
; Table: 6.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"It shall be present if the result of the ME Identity Check is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ecr-user-name-imsi
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: ME-Identity-Check-Request
; Section: 6.2.1.1
; Table: 6.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This information element shall contain the user IMSI, formatted according to TS 23.003 [3], clause 2.2."
    encoding digits
    length 6..15 digits


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: eca-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: ME-Identity-Check-Answer
; Section: 6.2.1.1
; Table: 6.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ecr-terminal-information
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Command: ME-Identity-Check-Request
; Section: 6.2.1.1
; Table: 6.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Within this Information Element, only the IMEI and the Software-Version AVPs shall be used on the S13/S13' interface."
    members only IMEI Software-Version


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ecr-terminal-information-imei
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Command: ME-Identity-Check-Request
; Section: 6.2.1.2
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Terminal-Information, when sent by the MME/SGSN to the EIR, shall contain the IMEI AVP, and it may contain also the Software-Version AVP."
    members at-least-one IMEI


;; Clause 7.1.4: the S6a/S6d and S13/S13' sessions are implicitly
;; terminated, in each command of the two applications; S7a/S7d's, between
;; the MME or SGSN and the CSS, the clause does not name.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 7.1.4
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [61]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 7.1.4
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ulr-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Update-Location-Request
; Section: 7.1.4
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 7.1.4
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [61]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ula-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Update-Location-Answer
; Section: 7.1.4
; Versions: 18.7.0..19.6.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


